# Gitignored files Claude Code copies into every worktree it creates
# (`claude --worktree`, the EnterWorktree tool, subagent isolation:
# "worktree"). gitignore syntax. Only files that are BOTH matched here AND
# gitignored are copied; tracked files are already in the checkout. So with
# `Harness: committed` these lines are mostly no-ops, and with
# `Harness: local` (.claude/ gitignored) they are the only reason a worktree
# has a CLAUDE.md, settings.json (permissions, hooks, status line), hooks,
# skills and commands at all — a worktree reads them from its own root, with
# no fallback to the main checkout. Details: .claude/README.md §4.
#
# Explicit allowlist on purpose: a blanket `.claude/` also copies
# .claude/worktrees/ (nested checkouts) and .claude/logs/, and negation
# patterns (`!.claude/logs/`) were ignored (verified 2026-09-16, CLI 2.1.260).
.claude/CLAUDE.md
.claude/CUSTOM.md
.claude/README.md
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agents/
.claude/commands/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/scripts/
.claude/skills/

# Per-project additions go below, e.g. `.env` / `.env.local`. Copies land
# inside the worktree, which shares the parent's .gitignore, so they stay
# untracked there too.
